<font size=5>Gibler Floodplain Survey</font>
<br>
<i>UI Eco-Hydraulics Group (UI)</i>
<p>

Steve C. and Gloria walked the channel and floodplain portions of the Gibler property and selected the best cross section locations to describe the channel shape.  A total of 25 cross section locations were marked with short wood stakes and flagging and labeled with writing.  Gloria also drew a color map marking the positions of the cross section stakes to help locate the stakes in the future.  The locations of these cross section end points will be permanently monumented and surveyed in October.
<p>
Based upon this survey information and aerial photos, Steve C., Gloria, Denny Dawes (WHI), Steve Bauer (PWI) and Peter Goodwin (UI) will delineate the area of greatest interest on the Gibler property.  CE Engineering will then focus their surveying effort on that portion of the floodplain most appropriate for monitoring the restoration in the rest of the meadow.  
<p>
<b>Note:</b> Steve C. and Denny met with Sara Jo (Gibler) and Don Johnson to discuss the plans for the coming months before starting any of the survey work on the Gibler property.  At the meeting, Steve and Denny hand-delivered a letter from UI which outlined how and when the cross section and floodplain surveying would be completed.  Linda Klein (LRK) will forward copies of the letter to other members of the Gibler family.
<p>
