<font size=5>Education/Public Information</font>
<br>
<i>UI Eco-Hydraulics Group (UI)</i>
<p>
Steve Clayton and Peter Goodwin are scheduling a meeting with Kit Freudenberg at the Idaho Fish and Wildlife Foundation regarding sources of funding to enhance the educational facilities at Red River WMA.  
<p>
<a href="mailto:jabbott@uidaho.edu">Jason Abbott</a> updated our project's web page to include the <a href="1998-07_1.asp">July newsletter</a>.
<p>
Coordinates from all previous surveys of the meadow are being converted into "real world" coordinates (i.e., UTM) so that the data can be linked to and shared with other sources.

<hr size="2" color=<%=color1%>>

<font size=5>Planting Activities</font>
<br>
<i>Wildlife Habitat Institute (WHI)</i>
<p>
Kurt Dostal, WHI Restoration Manager, maintained irrigation on willow cuttings and herbaceous seedlings through the month of August.  Irrigation equipment was moved periodically in order to cover all planted areas.
<p>
Kurt also collected seed including beaked sedge (<i>Carex rostrata</i>), small-wing sedge (<i>C. microptera</i>), Colorado rush (<i>Juncus confusus</i>), jointed rush (<i>J. articulatus</i>), dagger-leaf rush (<i>J. ensifolius</i>), Baltic rush (<i>J. balticus</i>), and camas (<i>Camassia quamash</i>). 

